- Sure, contracts are the backbone of your business relationships. Want me to suggest the key ones for your stage? For early startups, you definitely need a founder agreement covering equity split, roles, and vesting – like a 4-year vesting with a 1-year cliff. NDAs for everyone you talk to. Employment or contractor agreements for your team, including IP assignment. Terms of use and privacy policy for your website or app. If you're providing services, an SLA. Shareholders agreement if you have investors. And vendor agreements for partners. I can help draft templates for these.